--------------------- Props -----------------------

Used to pass data from parent to child

Data is passed manually at each level

Best suited for direct parent–child communication

Easy to understand and implement

No extra setup required

Can cause prop drilling when data is needed deep in the component tree

Better for small, localized data

Does not cause unnecessary re-renders


----------------- Context API ---------------

Used to share data globally

Data is accessed directly by any component inside Provider

Best suited for app-level/global data

Requires setup (createContext, Provider, useContext)

Solves the prop drilling problem

Ideal for theme, authentication, language, settings

Overuse may cause performance issues (extra re-renders)

Not recommended for frequently changing data